msgid "{v}, as in {word}"
msgstr "{v}, as in {word}"

msgid "<0/> is a hundred; <1/> means send. A double letter is a longer sound, and it makes a different word. Consonants work the same way: <2/> is a hen, and <3/> tells one person to carry something."
msgstr "<0/> is a hundred; <1/> means send. A double letter is a longer sound, and it makes a different word. Consonants work the same way: <2/> is a hen, and <3/> tells one person to carry something."

